# FCM & Notifications

## Purpose

Keep push + in-app notifications reliably wired to session lifecycle.

## When Applied

Editing notifications, app bootstrap, or auth sign-out.

## Requirements

- `NotificationBloc` + FCM are wired through `AuthenticatedShell` — authenticated UI must enter via the shell.
- FCM token is stored on `profiles.fcm_token`; refresh on login, **clear on sign-out**.
- Notification realtime subscriptions are disposed on sign-out (see [`data/auth-boundary.mdc`](../data/auth-boundary.mdc)).
- Notification data access stays in the notifications repository (see [`data/repository-boundary.mdc`](../data/repository-boundary.mdc)).
- Context: [`ai/context/notifications.md`](../../../ai/context/notifications.md).

## Examples

- Sign-out path → clear `profiles.fcm_token`, dispose realtime, then Supabase sign-out.

## Anti-patterns

- Registering FCM outside the shell, so some entry paths miss it.
- Leaving a stale token on a device after logout.

## Common Mistakes

- Handling FCM token writes in a widget instead of the repository.
- Realtime subscription leaks across account switches.
